Part 1: The Core Concepts & Architecture

    `1. Decoupled Architecture (Client-Server)

        What it is: Separating your application into two distinct pieces: the "Brain" (Backend/Server)
                    and the "Face" (Frontend/Client).

        How we did it: We put your AI logic, FastAPI, and ChromaDB on Render (The Brain). Then, we built separate
                       apps using Streamlit and Discord on your computer (The Faces).

        Usage/Example: Think of a restaurant. Render is the Kitchen. It only cooks data. Streamlit is
                       the Waiter in the dining room, and Discord is the Drive-Thru window. Because the Kitchen
                       is independent, both the Waiter and the Drive-Thru can order food from it at the exact same time.

        🚧 Problem we faced: Initial Confusion. You asked, "Why do we even need Render if Streamlit can run Python?"
                              We solved this by realizing that if we trapped the AI inside Streamlit, Discord would
                              never be able to talk to it.

